# apps.rst, thread_latency (M3): sem, nopreempt mode.
# Schematic: the box widths fit the labels, they are not durations.
include apps.tdc
diagram thread-latency-nopreempt "thread_latency, sem-nopreempt: the taker runs only when the giver blocks"
schematic
prio taker 3
axis "time after the giver wakes (schematic)" -30..750

taker pending -30.. "blocked in k_sem_take()"
giver -30..0 : The ISR of the edge woke the giver. The giver took t_thr.
at 0
giver 36 "now" : t0 = stim_now(), just before the wake call.
@t0
giver 96 "k_sem_give()" : The wake call makes the taker ready. The taker has the lower priority, so there is no switch.
giver 36 "now" : t2 = stim_now(): the wake call has returned.
@t2
giver 115 "record previous" : The giver records t2t and t2t_ret of the previous edge, then calls giver_prepare().
giver 82 "stim_arm()" {basepri} : Programs the next edge.
giver 96 "k_sem_take()" : Blocks for the next edge.
@giver_blocks anchor
giver pending giver_blocks..750 "blocked in k_sem_take(isr_sem)"
pendsv 56 "switch" : Giver to taker.
taker 36 "now" : t1 = stim_now(), the first action after k_sem_take() returns.
@t1
taker 96 "k_sem_take()" : The taker counts the wake and blocks again.
@taker_blocks anchor
taker pending taker_blocks..750 "blocked"
pendsv 56 "switch" : Taker to the idle thread.
@idle_runs anchor
idle sleep idle_runs..750 "WFI"
span t0..t2 "t2t_ret" !
span t0..t1 "t2t" !
